diet: Vegetarian
tags: mini cheesecakes, mascarpone cheesecake, berries, no bake, easy, gluten free
cuisine: American
time required: 1 hour
servings: 8
source: https://www.forkknifeswoon.com/no-bake-mascarpone-mini-cheesecakes/
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
---

== Make the graham cracker base ==

Use a #food processor{} to pulse together @graham crackers{1%cup}(finely crushed), @brown sugar{3%tbsp}(light, packed), @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @ground cinnamon{1/4%tsp}.

Drizzle in @butter{1/4%cup}(unsalted, melted) and pulse a few times until combined.

Divide the base between your jars or serving dishes. Press down gently into an even layer. Set aside.

== Make the mascarpone cheesecake filling ==

Add @heavy whipping cream{1%cup}(chilled) to the #stand mixer{} fitted with the balloon whisk attachment. Starting on low speed, and gradually increasing, beat the cream until soft, fluffy peaks form, about ~{7%minutes}. Transfer the whipped cream to a separate bowl.

Add @mascarpone cheese{8%oz}(room-temperature) and @sugar{1/2%cup} to the mixing bowl, and beat together until light and creamy and no lumps remain.

Beat in @vanilla extract{1%tsp}() and the zest of one @lemon{}(can replace with a splash of lemon juice and a pinch of sugar).

Use a spatula to gently and methodically fold the whipped cream into the mascarpone mixture until combined.

Divide the mascarpone cheesecake filling between the jars. It may be easier to fill a large pastry bag and pipe the filling into the cups. Refrigerate until ready to serve.

== Make the topping and assemble ==

Stir together @strawberries{1/2%cup}(chopped), @blueberries{1/2%cup}, and @pitted cherries{1/2%cup} with @sugar{2%tbsp} and @lemon juice{1%tsp}(). Let sit for at least ~{30%minutes}.

Top the cheesecake with the fruit and syrup shortly before serving.